And let me bear with thee a kindness I do not love.
   So that I may love thee in all my heart,
  So that thou mayst bear me a kindness I do not love.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Thy own grace of love free from sin,
That my sins shall be thy fairest reward.
Thou art my love and my love my sweet heart;
Thy sweetest possession is my poor love,
Which in thee is love's state, though not perfect.
  But thou art my love, and love's love art mine.
  O, then thou shalt love me; and love's love shall be my delight,
  Which thou shalt do with love, and do not love with love,



Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
His love's flight and the carelessness of her
Prevent his sweet vows, which nature loves so,
To set her down with a slave, to return
To those that love her with love's sweetest tenderness.
Therefore she's ruined and her sweet friends disgraced.
But I have heard of them, and I hold no ill grudge.


